	<h2>The Mission</h2>
	<p>
		<strong>ErrorLedger is the internet's universal systems analysis engine.</strong>
	</p>
	<p>
		We do not publish hype, press releases, or generic summaries. Instead, we perform forensic, evidence-grounded systems audits across two core domains:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Distributed & Technical Systems:</strong> Hardware scaling limits, LLM runtime architectures, kernel bottlenecks, distributed database consistency failures, and platform outages.</li>
		<li><strong>Biological & Lifestyle Systems:</strong> Viral wellness claims, physiological protocols, recovery mechanisms, habit economics, and behavioral interventions audited against controlled trials.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Our Core Philosophy: Everything is a System</h2>
	<p>
		We operate under a simple axiom: <em>every physical, digital, and physiological process is a system operating under real-world constraints.</em> A viral recovery protocol is a biological system. An agent runtime is a distributed system. A high-frequency trading pipeline is a probabilistic system.
	</p> 
	<p>
		By auditing the <strong>Inputs &rarr; Transformation &rarr; Outputs &rarr; Constraints</strong> of every subject, we diagnose structural failure boundaries and separate empirical reality from marketed expectations.
	</p>

	<h2>The Systems Audit Framework</h2>
	<p>
		Every analysis published on ErrorLedger adheres to a strict editorial contract:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Primary Evidence Sourcing:</strong> Every assertion is linked to primary sources (from Tier-1 incident RCAs and architecture specs to Cochrane systematic reviews and randomized controlled trials).</li>
		<li><strong>Separation of Fact and Inference:</strong> We explicitly demarcate directly observed empirical data from analytical deductions and engineering inferences.</li>
		<li><strong>Constraint-Driven Viability:</strong> We analyze where systems thrive, where they bottleneck, and where they structurally fail.</li>
		<li><strong>Reusable Diagnostic Assets:</strong> Every post delivers production-ready engineering or physiological diagnostic tools (Python calculators, Prometheus alerting rules, parsers, and verification matrices).</li>
		<li><strong>Revision Triggers:</strong> We document known unknowns and establish explicit data triggers for re-auditing our conclusions.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Editorial Independence & Scoring</h2>
	<p>
		ErrorLedger operates with complete editorial independence. Every subject is evaluated using a standardized rubric—scoring Technical Soundness/Biological Plausibility, Evidence Quality, Scalability/Effect Magnitude, Operational Simplicity/Sustainability, and Implementation Cost—ensuring conclusions are grounded strictly in evidence, not bias.
	</p>
